<a name="FANTADV">
<h2>Fantastic Adventures</h2>

From <I>Tuck's Encyclopedia of Science Fiction and Fantasy</I>:
<p>
<pre>
      This magazine was begun by Palmer as a companion to <i>Amazing Stories</i> and 
    was large size to emulate the early <i>Amazing</i>; this did not last long.  It 
    published much light "frothy" fantasy in its early years, but by the late 
    1940's was printing much the same material as its companion, only more 
    fantastic in vein. At one stage in the very early 1940's it nearly ceased. 
    Some novels around 1950-1951 were of importance, but the story standard 
    dropped considerably in its last year. Its position as companion to <i>Amazing</i> 
    was taken by <i>Fantastic</i>.
</pre>
